<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-AUSTRIA'S GOETSCHL WINS COMBINED.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-AUSTRIA'S GOETSCHL WINS COMBINED.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Renate Goetschl of Austria won the women's combined gold medal at the Alpine skiing world championships on Saturday in a total time of three minutes 3.38 seconds, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Katja Seizinger of Germany won the silver medal in 3:03.42 and Hilde Gerg of Germany was third in 3:03.46.</p>
</text>
